        {
            "id": "110911831191242845",
            "user_id": "109400021060822669",
            "content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.au/@Bellingen\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>Bellingen</span></a></span> all that yes, AND, there were 80+ mph downdraft  winds that came off the mountain unexpectedly, snapped power poles at the base, most likely igniting the fires, and cutting off power to the pumps that are key to that part of Maui's water system causing fire hydrants to go dry.  Doesn't negate what you are saying, but it is a more complex cascade of failures.</p><p><a href=\"https://twitter.com/KanekoaTheGreat/status/1690833566694100992\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">twitter.com/KanekoaTheGreat/st</span><span class=\"invisible\">atus/1690833566694100992</span></a></p>"
        },
